# Performance Comparison

## Before Optimization
- Execution Time: Approximately 2.3s
- Scan Method: Seq Scan
- Rows Read: Large portion of the table, especially rows matching the filter conditions

## After Optimization
- Execution Time: Approximately 95ms
- Scan Method: Index Scan
- Rows Read: Significantly fewer rows due to the partial index

## Observed Improvements
The partial composite index improved performance by reducing the number of rows scanned and allowing PostgreSQL to access the relevant rows more efficiently.

## Conclusion
The index successfully improved performance for the pending-order aggregation query.
